ever since the fbi raid on donald  trump's home in florida a couple of  weeks ago we've been following the right  wings attempt to throw everything at the  wall and see what sticks as it pertains  to excuses for the former president and  they really have tried everything right  they've tried saying that the fbi  planted evidence they tried saying that  trump was cooperating so you didn't have  to do this they tried saying that this  is just not how you treat a former  president and this is a political witch  hunt all of these different excuses  right but now we've got a new one and it  comes to us from  rudy giuliani who as we know is facing  enough problems right now because he is  the target of that election fraud  lawsuit in georgia rudy went on newsmax  and made the case that it was totally  fine that donald trump had those  documents with him down in mar-a-lago  locked away in the basement because they  were just as safe there as they would  have been at a government facility and  that's exactly why  he should be able to get away with this  without any consequences let's take a  look at the video of rudy making a fool  of himself  and and now  they want to make him responsible for  having taken classified documents  and preserved them really if you look at  the espionage act it's not really about  taking the documents  it's about destroying them or hiding  them  or giving them to the enemy right it's  not about taking them and putting them  in a place  that's roughly as safe as they were in  the first place well to be fair to rudy  giuliani when hillary clinton's email  scandal was in focus he was actually  saying the exact same thing like he  would go on tv and he would talk about  how the emails stored on a private  server those are roughly as safe as they  would be if stored through the proper  channels of the government oh wait no he  actually he didn't say those things  funny how there's a double standard  between donald trump and hillary clinton  on this issue but what's funny about  this clip is that rudy actually debunks  himself in real time because he says  that if you look at the espionage act  it's not about taking documents it's  about hiding them destroying them or  giving them to the enemy well what  exactly is donald trump being  investigating for if not for hiding the  documents he brought them to mar-a-lago  and he hid them in the basement uh so  definitely debunking his own argument  there is rudy giuliani and then we also  know that trump liked to destroy  documents we've heard stories about him  ripping up documents we've seen the  pictures of him flushing the documents  supposedly 10 to 15 times and even  eating a document as omarosa alleges but  rudy manages in this clip to be wrong  about something else too which is pretty  impressive because there was only a 30  second clip that i showed you um which  is that he was wrong about the espionage  act and what it says let's take a look  at the espionage act it says whoever  lawfully having possession of access to  control over or being entrusted with any  document writing code book signal book  sketch photograph photographic negative  blueprint plan map model instrument  appliance or note relating to the  national defense or information relating  to the national defense which  information the possessor has reason to  believe could be used to the injury of  the united states or to the advantage of  any foreign nation willfully  communicates delivers transmits or  causes to be communicated delivered or  transmitted or attempts to communicate  deliver transmit or cause to be  communicated delivered or transmitted  the same to any person not entitled to  receive it or willfully retains the same  and fails to deliver it on demand to the  officer or employee of the united states  entitled to receive it okay so that's  some impressively verbose legal jargon  there but if you cut through the fat you  see possession of access to or control  over defense information and then also  being unwilling to hand it over to the  proper authorities who are entitled to  it that's a violation of the espionage  act so rudy would have been better  served to read the law that he was  talking about before going on newsmax  and spewing nonsense about it on their  airwaves and then finally how are we to  believe that these documents were safer  than they would have been than at a  government facility or just as safe  because why they had a lock on them in  the basement at mar-a-lago is that the  argument you want to make so the  staffers at mar-a-lago the maintenance  people the custodians they could  probably get at least around that area  you best believe they don't have  security clearances so how is that in  any proper way the proper handling of  documents it's clearly not and then  we've also heard about how nonchalant  trump was when it pertained to sensitive  information at mar-a-lago while he was  president even making an impromptu  situation room on the patio at  mar-a-lago after north korea tested a  missile launch with guests of the resort  just walking by able to see exactly what  was being talked about between the  president and his team and remember  shinzo abe the late former japanese  prime minister was also there he must  have been absolutely shocked by the  entire thing so all the excuses from the  right for trump on this have been bad  they seem to be getting worse actually  we may at some point have to drop a  formal list of all of the horrible  excuses and rank them from best to worst  and my prediction is that this latest  one from rudy giuliani that the  documents were roughly as safe as they  would have been in a government facility  that has to be pretty high on the list  all right we're going to go to a break  now but we'll be back with much more of  the david pakman show right after this
 

